.tbtn.small { width: 62px; height: 62px; font-size: 19px; }
```
But grid items are `.tbtn` with global width; grid also. Right cluster children: strike, switch, action, jump. Order grid: strike, switch / action, jump. Jump at bottom-right; good. Maybe highlight jump. Could reorder DOM to put action+jump? Keep.

Left cluster: two dir buttons 70 each + gap 10 =150. Right grid 62*2+10=134. Total 284 + padding 24 =308 <390. Even 320-wide phones fine. Great.

Maybe make buttons bigger for thumbs: right cells 66, left 72: 72*2+10=154, right 66*2+10=142, total 296+24=320. Fits 320 exactly tight. Use 64: right 138; dir 70: left 150; total 288+24=312. Good. Use these.

Also add a background to the lower area so it's not pure black: `background: radial-gradient(80% 60% at 50% 10%, rgba(24,48,36,0.5), rgba(4,12,8,0.9) 70%);` on .touch in portrait maybe. But .touch has transparent gradient. Let's set the app background to radial; it already has. The lower area appears black because #stage ends and #app background gradient is dark. Add `#app::after`? Simpler: in portrait, give body/app a subtle gradient; or `.touch` background gradient from stage edge into dark. Current `.touch` background linear-gradient transparent→rgba(4,12,8,.5) 30%. Screenshot shows black anyway. Fine, but we can add a faint grid/path. Not necessary.

Also the HUD objective on mobile overlaps chapter label? It's at top 64; location label at top 12; no.

