content.text:
Journal is clean now. Mobile title fills whole screen but the bottom half is still very dark/black because the canvas is only in top 58% and the title-copy is flex-start with the background repeating? Actually the .screen fixed covers full viewport with a gradient, but underlying canvas only 490 tall. The screen background is radial+linear gradient — it appears black at bottom because it's mostly opaque dark. Hmm, the title mark is at bottom right faint. It's acceptable but could be better: center the title copy vertically on mobile for titles? Currently title-copy align-self flex-start p-top 10vh, buttons around 360-500. Black from 540-844. There's title-mark decoration in bottom. It's not terrible, but the black band at 540–844 looks like empty. The screen background is dark gradient, expected. Could instead allow canvas/title art fill 100dvh on title screen only. Simplest: when title screen active, stage height should be 100dvh? That requires JS toggling class on app. Alternatively, CSS can't detect which screen. Could add body class 'at-title' set by showTitle. Hmm.

Alternative: on mobile portrait, make #stage height 100dvh for screens but the game should be 58dvh during play. We can set a class on #app e.g. `.menu-open` toggled from ui.showScreen/hideScreens. Simpler: in UI showScreen, add document.body.dataset.screen = name; hideScreens delete. Then CSS:
```
@media portrait... {
  body[data-screen="title"] #stage, body[data-screen="intro"] #stage, body[data-screen="interlude"] #stage { height: 100dvh; flex: 1; margin-top:0; }
}
```
But when title screen active, #stage full height, canvas backing is only 490 tall? Renderer resizes to stage; at boot stage measured height maybe 58dvh then when class applies after render? On resize observer would catch size change. Might be flaky.

Better approach for mobile title: use a CSS background for the screen that extends the art? Could set `.title-screen` background to a richer gradient and reposition title copy to center. The current black area shows decorative title mark at bottom right. Honestly acceptable but let's improve by vertically centering title-copy on portrait instead of flex-start, with h1 etc. If centered, content from ~170 to ~680, still some black. Actually with fixed screen, center gives buttons around y=500-650 and art on top? Title copy is overlay with h1. The art top 490 remains visible behind top part. It'd look more balanced.

But the menu buttons at 400ish are over characters artwork, overlapping bodies. Centering would move buttons below art onto dark area and title across art. Let's set `.title-copy { align-self: center; padding-top: 0; }` on portrait. The title is 54-100px; 3 lines? Title occupies ~150, sub ~50, buttons ~170, total ~400; centered leaves 220 top and bottom. The art (bright sky/moon) is top 0-300 and city 300-490, characters at 480. Text over moon possibly. Hmm.

Maybe the real fix: make the title screen canvas fill viewport on mobile. We can do it with JS when title visible: call resize? Let's inspect main.js and resize observer. Perhaps we can just set #stage to 100dvh when `body` has class `menu`, then renderer canvas resizes. But then when gameplay starts, switch class and canvas resizes. That's a nice look for title/intro/interlude/ending? For gameplay, stage 58dvh.

Let's inspect main.js/UI show functions to implement cleanly.

